). Though, individually, the two words of the compound (iṣṭa and पूर्त) mean, ‘what is sacrificed’ and ‘what is filled’ the total sense seems to be: cumulative spiritual result or merit due to a man’s performance of sacrifices and charitable acts.
‘Iṣṭa’ includes all types of वेदिच् सच्रिड़िचेस्, including the gifts given during its performance.
‘Pūrta’ indicates the various acts of charity and public utility such as: building and dedicating of deep wells for the good of the public, building temples and gardens, free distribution of ड़ोओद्, giving gifts, nursing the sick and many other acts of charity sanctioned by the holy books.
